# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and fill in. Never commit a real .env file.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are embedded in the JS bundle IN PLAINTEXT.
# They are for base URLs and feature flags ONLY.
# No secret, key, credential or token may ever be an EXPO_PUBLIC_ variable.
#
# The Razorpay PUBLISHABLE key is deliberately absent from this file: the backend returns it
# per-order as `keyId` on `POST /v1/bookings/:id/payments/order`, so the app never ships one.

# development | staging | production
APP_ENV=development

# The Spoon API root, WITHOUT a trailing slash and WITHOUT the `/v1` prefix — every feature
# module spells its own `/v1/...` path, so the base URL is the host only.
#
#   Deployed (Render):   https://spoon-api-kalc.onrender.com
#   Local, USB device:   http://127.0.0.1:3000     + `adb reverse tcp:3000 tcp:3000`
#   Local, Android emu:  http://10.0.2.2:3000
#   Local, LAN:          http://<your-lan-ip>:3000 (backend must bind 0.0.0.0)
#
# `adb reverse` is preferred on a physical handset: it needs no LAN, survives a changing IP, and
# means the backend can keep listening on loopback. Note that on a device "localhost" is the
# PHONE, not this machine — which is exactly what `adb reverse` fixes.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://spoon-api-kalc.onrender.com

# Request timeout in milliseconds.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# debug | info | warn | error | silent
EXPO_PUBLIC_LOG_LEVEL=debug

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Maps Platform
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two CLIENT keys, one per platform. They are NOT EXPO_PUBLIC_ variables: they are read by
# app.config.ts and delivered three ways —
#
#   Maps SDK for Android  -> AndroidManifest.xml `com.google.android.geo.API_KEY`
#   Maps SDK for iOS      -> Info.plist + the GoogleMaps AppDelegate init
#   Places (New)/Geocoding -> `extra`, because those are HTTPS APIs called from JS
#
# The last one means the key IS readable in a shipped build. That is true of every client that
# calls Google's web APIs directly, and it is why each key MUST carry an application restriction
# in Google Cloud — the restriction, not secrecy, is what makes a client key safe:
#
#   Android key : Application restriction = "Android apps"
#                 package  com.spoonhelp.userapp.dev      (development)
#                          com.spoonhelp.userapp          (production)
#                 SHA-1    the signing certificate of the build (see ANDROID_SIGNING_SHA1 below)
#   iOS key     : Application restriction = "iOS apps"
#                 bundle   com.spoonhelp.userapp.dev      (development)
#                          com.spoonhelp.customer         (production — the Apple App ID, which
#                          deliberately DIFFERS from the Android package; see app.config.ts)
#   Both keys   : API restriction = Maps SDK (its platform) + Places API (New) + Geocoding API
#
# The BACKEND's Google Routes key is separate, lives on the backend, and must never appear here.
#
# A build with no keys still works: the map and search report themselves unavailable and the rest
# of the address flow (device position, OS reverse geocoding, serviceability, saving) continues.
# A PRODUCTION build refuses to start without them.
GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_MAPS_IOS_API_KEY=

# The signing certificate SHA-1 of the build, uppercase hex (separators are stripped for you).
# Sent as `X-Android-Cert` alongside `X-Android-Package` so an "Android apps"-restricted key
# accepts the Places/Geocoding REST calls — the native SDKs send these headers themselves, a REST
# caller has to. OPTIONAL: leave blank until the key is actually restricted.
#
#   debug build : keytool -list -v -keystore android/app/debug.keystore -storepass android \
#                   -alias androiddebugkey
#   any APK     : apksigner verify --print-certs <apk>
#
# This machine's debug keystore is 5E:8F:16:06:2E:A3:CD:2C:4A:0D:54:78:76:BA:A6:F3:8C:AB:F6:25.
# The RELEASE keystore has a different one — set this per build.
ANDROID_SIGNING_SHA1=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Push notifications (Android / FCM)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PATH to the Firebase `google-services.json` for this build's Android package. Read by
# app.config.ts and written into the native project as `android.googleServicesFile`.
#
# NOT the file's contents, and NOT committed: it carries the Firebase project identifiers and is
# regenerated per package (`com.spoonhelp.userapp.dev` in development, without `.dev` for release).
# Leave it blank and the app still builds and runs — `expo-notifications` then cannot obtain a
# device token, the provider reports "no token", and registration is skipped rather than a
# fabricated token reaching `PUT /v1/me/push-token`.
#
# iOS has no equivalent line here: APNs is configured by uploading a key to EAS, not by a file in
# the project.
GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON=
